00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:01.837
WESLEY CHUN: Welcome
to part three

00:00:01.837 --> 00:00:04.680
of our series on using G Suite
APIs for student developers.

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:06.930
This is developer
advocate, Wesley Chun.

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:09.960
Previously, we discussed how
to use G Suite REST APIs.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:12.510
Now, we'll switch gears
to show you a higher level

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:14.430
way of accessing those APIs.

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:16.290
We'll switch from
Python to JavaScript

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:19.530
and drop all the security code,
as it's automatically generated

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:21.180
for you by Google Apps Script.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:22.620
So what is Apps Script?

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:24.810
Well, I think of it as
another Google secret.

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:26.940
But it's actually not
a secret, nor is it

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:29.670
well kept, since it's been
out for over a decade.

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:30.630
It is JavaScript.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:34.020
But instead of using
REST and HTTP with OAuth,

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:37.125
you use built-in objects
to talk to Google APIs.

00:00:37.125 --> 00:00:39.000
Also, you don't have to
write the OAuth code,

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.660
because it's automatically
generated for you.

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:43.980
Now while it is
server-side like node,

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:46.680
it's more like using JavaScript
as a programming language,

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:50.350
rather than for a synchronous
event-driven web apps.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:53.380
Now a one liner describing
Apps Script looks like this.

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:56.970
It's serverless, meaning no
VMs, because we host and run

00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:58.020
your code.

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:00.270
It helps automate
repeated tasks,

00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:03.150
extends the functionality
of G Suite editors,

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:05.340
connects to non-Google
Cloud products,

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:07.530
like maps, analytics
and YouTube.

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:09.840
And lets you access
external databases

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:12.070
or other online services.

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:13.980
Now let's get started
with a Google Sheet.

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:17.370
It's got many functions,
